    "create_time": 1791775221.41,
    "update_time": 1791775223.8032837,
    "content": {
     "content_type": "text",
     "parts": [
      "**Two days out (Tue–Wed): carb load-lite**\nFor a ~85-minute race you don't need a full marathon load, but topping up glycogen helps.\n- ~7–8 g/kg/day → **460–530 g carbs/day**.\n- Mostly low-fiber: white rice, bagels, pasta, potatoes without skin, juice, pretzels, bananas.\n- Reduce fat and fiber a bit so the total isn't a huge food volume. Keep protein normal.\n\n**Race morning (start time assumed ~7:30)**\n- 3–3.5 h before: **~2 g/kg ≈ 130 g carbs.** E.g., bagel + honey + banana + small juice. Things you've eaten before long runs.\n- Sip ~500 ml water/electrolyte by 1 h before, then small sips.\n- 15 min before the start: **1 gel (~25 g)** with water.\n\n**During**\n- At 1:25 race time, a gel at **~35–40 min** (around mile 5) is enough; optionally a second at ~60 min if your stomach handles it.\n- Take each with a cup of water at an aid station.\n\n**Don't try anything new.** Use the same gel brand you trained with and the same breakfast as your last long run."
     ]
    },
